BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Unscripted
DTSTART:20261110T230000
DTEND:20261111T000000
DTSTAMP:20261108T173323Z
UID:c0fec4a0f3b2dd405a8fee2ead8e7a@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Let’s Flip the Script: Challenge gender expectations\, break
  the stereotypes\, and make space for everyone to be their authentic selve
 s. Let’s Flip the Script is a discussion-based program designed to encou
 rage participants to critically examine traditional expectations\, gender 
 roles\, and social norms that can influence how people are expected to loo
 k\, act\, communicate\, and express themselves. Throughout the program\, p
 articipants will explore the different “scripts” that society can plac
 e on people based on gender. Through videos\, reflection\, and group discu
 ssion\, we’ll examine messages such as “be a man\,” “men shouldn
 ’t show emotion\,” “women should look or act a certain way\,” and 
 other expectations that can limit how people feel they are allowed to be. 
 Participants will watch videos featuring men discussing the societal expec
 tations and unwritten rules often associated with masculinity\, followed b
 y a clip from Miss Representation exploring the expectations and roles tha
 t society has historically placed on women. Together\, we’ll discuss how
  these messages can impact people of all genders and consider what it migh
 t look like to challenge the script\, embrace individuality\, and create s
 pace for everyone to be themselves. --- Event Details: https://myhc.holycr
 oss.edu/rsvp?id=2154159 Source: College of the Holy Cross Event page: http
 s://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154159\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles 
 of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from worcester-colle
 ges-events.ics\nSource page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154159
LOCATION:Hogan Center 4th Floor Room 408(09)\, The College of the Holy Cro
 ss\, Hogan Campus Center- Suite 506\, Worcester\, MA 01610\, United States
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154159
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Unsettling Hospitality: A Dialogue Dinner Event
DTSTART:20261110T223000
DTEND:20261111T000000
DTSTAMP:20261108T173323Z
UID:00112911fa47dfb5e4fa5006a8d365@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Join SPEECH and the Unsettling Hospitality faculty group for a
 n upcoming Dialogue Dinner exploring the meaning of hospitality on our cam
 pus and in the Worcester community. Together\, we will reflect on what it 
 means to welcome others\, create a sense of belonging\, and build a commun
 ity where people feel valued. Through conversation\, we will also consider
  how the campus’s new Private Property signs align with our individual a
 nd shared understandings of hospitality. How do we balance boundaries and 
 access with a commitment to welcoming others? Join us for an evening of th
 oughtful dialogue\, reflection\, and connection as we explore what hospita
 lity looks like in practice. --- Event Details: https://myhc.holycross.edu
 /rsvp?id=2154904 Source: College of the Holy Cross Event page: https://myh
 c.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154904\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Nort
 hborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from worcester-colleges-eve
 nts.ics\nSource page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154904
LOCATION:Hogan Suite B/C\, 1 College Street\, Worcester\, MA 01610\, Unite
 d States
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154904
END:VEVENT
