BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Open gallery hours: Small Works 2026 and Drinks on Me
DTSTART:20261112T000000
DTEND:20261213T000000
DTSTAMP:20261108T173323Z
UID:34fc77754ea9a520a8964895d5ec28@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:New exhibitions fill the ArtsWorcester galleries starting Nove
 mber 12\, and you won't want to miss all that's on view this holiday seaso
 n! In the East Gallery\, the annual favorite Small Works 2026 fills the sp
 ace with miniature works\, all measuring 10" x 10" or under. Artworks had 
 no medium or theme requirement\, making for a delightfully robust array of
  teeny treasures. Expect unique finds like an abstract turtle made from pl
 aster\, a miniature woven handbag\, a wooden bowl with the aura of a UFO\,
  and much more to be adored. Small works make unique holiday gifts\, too\,
  so you might find something perfect for someone in your life (or find som
 ething for your own personal collection)! In the West Gallery\, the solo s
 how Drinks on Me: interdisciplinary artist Amanda (Andi) Pickler explores 
 the spectrum of intimacy that exists within the domesticity of interperson
 al relationships\, and the public and private spaces of queer nightlife. P
 ickler's saturated\, jewel-toned paintings and detailed prints include sce
 nes from her trips to lesbian and queer bars around the country. These ima
 ges and the spaces they depict offer connection\, joy\, and respite to a c
 ommunity experiencing significant challenges and threats. Both exhibitions
  are on view starting November 12 through December 13 during gallery hours
 : Wednesdays through Sundays\, each day from 12pm to 5pm. On December 10\,
  ArtsWorcester will be open until 7 PM for late night hours. Gallery hours
  are always open and free to all. ArtsWorcester // 44 Portland Street\, Wo
 rcester\, MA 01608 On view November 12 - December 13 // Free and open to a
 ll // https://artsworcester.org/ Concurrently on view will be the Assets f
 or Artists 2026 Showcase in the third floor Davis Art Gallery. See our web
 site for more information on upcoming shows and events. Parking is availab
 le at the Worcester Public Library (McGrath) Lot\, Federal Plaza Garage\, 
 Worcester Common Garage\, and Pearl-Elm Garage. Metered street parking is 
 also available. On weekends\, and on weekdays after 5:00 PM\, visitors may
  park in the Printers Building parking lot free of charge. Please do not p
 ark in the lot across the street from the Printers Building\; you will be 
 immediately towed. // Photos: Andi Pickler\, They Don't Get To Tell Us Whe
 ther Or Not This Is Real\, oil on canvas\, 48" x 36"\, 2026 Andi Pickler\,
  Our Hands At Ginger's\, oil on panel\, 14" x 18"\, 2025 Sarah Beard\, It 
 Started to Clear Part Way Up\, 9" x 9"\, acrylic and collage\, 2025 Marjor
 ie Hart\, Hand woven purse with chain handle\, 8" x 8" x 0.5"\, 2024 Sourc
 es: Discover Central Massachusetts Event page: https://www.discovercentral
 ma.org/event/open-gallery-hours%3a-small-works-2026-and-drinks-on-me/31071
 /\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery
 : Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.d
 iscovercentralma.org/event/open-gallery-hours%3a-small-works-2026-and-drin
 ks-on-me/31071/
LOCATION:ArtsWorcester\, 44 Portland St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/open-gallery-hours%3a-small-wo
 rks-2026-and-drinks-on-me/31071/
END:VEVENT
