BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spotted Lanternfly Workshop
DTSTART:20261112T000000
DTEND:20261112T000000
DTSTAMP:20261108T173323Z
UID:0bba2df3c53f20e1f63d436662deaf@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Location: Banx Room Audience: Adult Register here: mywpl.org/e
 vent/17704005 This illustrated program looks at lessons learned since the 
 spotted lanternfly was first discovered in Pennsylvania in 2014\, what sci
 ence is still working to understand\, and what Worcester residents can rea
 listically do as the insect becomes established here. The emphasis is on p
 ractical management not eradication. Joe Johnson is a Worcester resident a
 nd a commissioner on the city’s Urban Forestry Tree Commission. He volun
 teers with the Blackstone Heritage Corridor and several local conservation
  and park stewardship organizations. With training in arboriculture\, inva
 sive plant management\, and pollinator stewardship\, Joe helps residents u
 nderstand invasive species through fieldwork\, public presentations\, and 
 community education. His spotted lanternfly program emphasizes lessons lea
 rned in other states and realistic approaches to managing this widespread 
 insect. Want to stay in the know about all things WPL? Sign up for our eNe
 wsletter! Program generously sponsored by the Friends of the Worcester Pub
 lic Library Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts Event page: https://ww
 w.discovercentralma.org/event/spotted-lanternfly-workshop/31164/\n\nEvents
  Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fal
 lback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.discovercent
 ralma.org/event/spotted-lanternfly-workshop/31164/
LOCATION:Worcester Public Library\, 3 Salem St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/spotted-lanternfly-workshop/31
 164/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The American Revolution on Trial
DTSTART:20261112T000000
DTEND:20261112T000000
DTSTAMP:20261108T173323Z
UID:da7d9aa905c44fdab31b04ac22b8cd@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:In this virtual talk\, T.H. Breen discusses his new book\, The
  American Revolution on Trial: A New Nation Confronts the Burden of Indepe
 ndence (March 2026)\, which reconstructs a strange court martial held in C
 ambridge\, Massachusetts in 1778. General John Burgoyne\, himself then a p
 risoner of war\, demanded that leading Continental officers try an honored
  American colonel for possible abuse of British soldiers. The trial was on
 ly marginally a military story. Rather\, it raised troublesome issues abou
 t achieving cultural independence from Great Britain--even during a war--a
 nd demonstrated how preserving the rule of law was important for people ea
 ger to establish an honorable reputation for the New Republic. Register fo
 r this virtual program here. T.H. Breen has written several prize-winning 
 books on the American Revolution\, including Marketplace of Revolution: Ho
 w Consumer Politics Shaped American Independence (2004)\, which won the Co
 lonial War Society Prize for the best book in 2004 on the American Revolut
 ion . Breen’s research and writing explore how the experiences of ordina
 ry Americans were as important as the actions of the Founding Fathers in m
 obilizing revolutionary resistance and achieving national independence. Br
 een has taught at Northwestern University\, the Universities of Oxford and
  Cambridge\, and at the California Institute of Technology. He was elected
  to AAS membership in April 1994. Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts 
 Event page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/the-american-revolutio
 n-on-trial/30658/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 
 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource pag
 e: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/the-american-revolution-on-tria
 l/30658/
LOCATION:American Antiquarian Society\, 185 Salisbury St.\, Worcester\, MA
 \, 01609
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/the-american-revolution-on-tri
 al/30658/
END:VEVENT
